**CT report** (written result), I can help interpret the wording. If it’s an actual **CT image/scan**, I may also be able to use a specialized **kidney imaging pipeline** as a preliminary signal, but it would **not** be a diagnosis.\n\n**Question 4/5:**  \nWhy was the CT scan done, and did the report mention anything about the **kidneys, cysts, masses, stones, lesions, or reduced kidney function**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03ebb2379b14a4eb0169ba9ffd4ddc8191acb207260f45cb88\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":359,"output":242,"cacheRead":9600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10201,"cost":{"input":0.0008975000000000001,"output":0.00363,"cacheRead":0.0024,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0069275}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773838328832}}
