dy**, and if needed **urology / radiology review**. AI image tools can be wrong, and a single extracted image is much less reliable than a full clinician-read CT.\n\n### Red flags / urgent concerns\nYou previously said you do **not** have:\n- blood in the urine\n- other obvious kidney symptoms\n\nThat is somewhat reassuring, but it does **not fully rule out** a kidney lesion.\n\n### Most likely interpretation right now\n- **Possibility 1:** the scan may truly contain a **kidney mass / tumor-like lesion** and needs proper clinical follow-up\n- **Possibility 2:** this may be a **false positive AI result**, especially if this is only one image slice or not the key kidney image from the exam\n- **Possibility 3:** the finding could represent something **non-cancerous** that still needs radiology interpretation, such as a cyst or another structural change\n\n### Confidence / uncertainty note\nI have **moderate concern** from the tool result, but **low confidence in any final conclusion** without the written CT report. The report matters much more than the model.\n\n**Question 5/5:**  \nCan you send me the **written CT report** or tell me **why the CT was done and exactly what the radiologist wrote about the kidneys**?\n\nIf you have the report, paste it here — that is the most important next step. After that, I can also give you a clearer combined explanation, and if you want, I can distill the symptom discussion plus this tool output into one patient-friendly summary.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03ebb2379b14a4eb0169baa0572c1c8191bd6cc52725c5153e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9684,"output":657,"cacheRead":16768,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27109,"cost":{"input":0.024210000000000002,"output":0.009855000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0041919999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.038257000000000006}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773838414798}}
